  The desktop
    The Super key (or the grid at the top left) opens the launcher.
    Right click on the background for a menu with the main tools.
    The power icon at the top right has the display scale and shutdown.
    Super+Enter opens a terminal, Super+Q closes a window,
    Alt+Tab switches windows, Print saves a screenshot to ~/Pictures.
    Ctrl+Alt+F2 has a second console, for logging in as root.
    The screen follows the size of the virtual machine's window. To pick
    a size yourself:  wlr-randr  lists outputs and modes, e.g.
      wlr-randr --output Virtual-1 --custom-mode 1920x1080

  Administration happens as root: run  su -  (or the "Root Terminal" program).
    snap now -c "note"     take a snapshot of the system
    snap list              list snapshots;  snap rewind  goes back
    worm status            protections at a glance
    worm fw allow 22       open a port in the firewall
    worm anon on           send all traffic through Tor
    bh open                a disposable sandbox for untrusted programs
    wh install htop        software from Debian, in a wormhole

  The terminal
    Grey text after the cursor is an earlier command: Right or End takes it.
    Up and Down go through earlier commands starting with what is typed;
    Ctrl+R searches them. Tab completes, also snapshot numbers and packages.
    Ctrl+Backspace deletes a word.  ls | clip copy  copies to the clipboard,
    clip paste  prints it (shared with the host in QEMU and virt-manager).

